# axcall ports file.
#
# Binds a short name to a transport, so "axcall radio gb7rdg" works with
# nothing else on the line. This is the replacement for /etc/ax25/axports,
# which named a callsign, a paclen and a window but no device, because
# kissattach bound the tty to the port name separately.
#
# Copy to /etc/axcall/ports for everyone, or ~/.config/axcall/ports for
# yourself; the per-user file replaces same-named entries in the system one.
#
# The first three columns are mandatory. "-" means "not set" in any of the
# optional ones, and anything after the window column is a description that is
# read by people and ignored by axcall. A command-line flag beats this file,
# which beats the built-in default.
#
# The transport column takes a serial device, optionally with a baud rate
# (the default is 57600), or a KISS-over-TCP host and port.
#
# After the window column you may set the KISS channel-access parameters that
# kissparms(8) used to set per interface: txdelay, persist, slottime and
# txtail. The three timers are in milliseconds, in steps of 10; persist is
# 0-255. Nothing is sent to the TNC unless you ask for it here or on the
# command line, so a TNC you have set up deliberately is left alone.

# name   callsign   transport            paclen  window  description
#radio   M0LTE-7    /dev/ttyUSB0:57600   256     4       144.800 MHz
#node    M0LTE-7    10.45.0.66:8001      -       -       LinBPQ

# With channel-access settings for a slow-keying radio:
#slow    M0LTE-7    /dev/ttyUSB1:9600    256     4       txdelay=500 persist=32 slottime=100   2m brick
